== G2  atomic state: which plane owns which fb, and is the CRTC active
-- /sys/kernel/debug/dri/1/state
plane[35]: plane-0
	crtc=crtc-0
	fb=40
crtc[37]: crtc-0
	enable=1
	active=1
-- /sys/kernel/debug/dri/fdec0000.ebc/state
plane[35]: plane-0
	crtc=crtc-0
	fb=40
crtc[37]: crtc-0
	enable=1
	active=1

G2 is CLOSED when the primary plane shows fb=0 or crtc=(null):
drm_atomic_helper_dirtyfb() then commits an empty state and returns 0.

It is ALSO closed, less obviously, when the plane holds a *different*
fb than the fbdev one -- e.g. a KMS compositor owning the plane. The
dirtyfb loop matches on identity, not on 'some plane is lit'. So the
owner of the plane's fb is the reading that matters:
/sys/kernel/debug/dri/1: plane fb=40, allocated by [fbcon]
  -> the fbdev framebuffer is on the plane; the fbdev damage path can reach it
/sys/kernel/debug/dri/fdec0000.ebc: plane fb=40, allocated by [fbcon]
  -> the fbdev framebuffer is on the plane; the fbdev damage path can reach it
